      "height": 630.0,
      "seed": 282361,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "One Tenant, One Identity\nThe provider signs in with a domain and the\nclient ID and secret of a machine-to-machine\napplication, or with a signed JWT, or with an\nAPI token ([provider configuration](https://gi\nthub.com/auth0/terraform-provider-auth0/blob/v\n1.63.0/docs/index.md#L48-L63)). It reads the\nvalues from environment variables such as\n`AUTH0_DOMAIN`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` and\n`AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET`.\n\nEvery call uses the scopes that this\napplication holds on the Management API. A\nmissing read scope does not cause an error;\nthe provider just reads an empty value. For\nexample, `client_secret` is an empty string\nunless the application has the\n`read:client_keys` scope ([credentials doc](ht\ntps://github.com/auth0/terraform-provider-auth\n0/blob/v1.63.0/docs/resources/client_credentia\nls.md#L182)). Connection options need the\nscopes `read:connections_options` and\n`update:connections_options` ([options scope](\nhttps://auth0.com/docs/troubleshoot/product-li\nfecycle/deprecations-and-migrations/migrate-co\nnnection-options-scope)).\n\nAuth0 recommends one tenant for each\nenvironment, such as development, staging and\nproduction ([multiple environments](https://au\nth0.com/docs/get-started/auth0-overview/create\n-tenants/set-up-multiple-environments)). The\nIDs of objects differ from tenant to tenant,\nso configurations refer to objects through\nresources or data sources, never through\ncopied IDs.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-2d12e7f90d02",
      "originalText": "One Tenant, One Identity\nThe provider signs in with a domain and the client ID and secret of a machine-to-machine application, or with a signed JWT, or with an API token ([provider configuration](https://github.com/auth0/terraform-provider-auth0/blob/v1.63.0/docs/index.md#L48-L63)). It reads the values from environment variables such as `AUTH0_DOMAIN`, `AUTH0_CLIENT_ID` and `AUTH0_CLIENT_SECRET`.\n\nEvery call uses the scopes that this application holds on the Management API. A missing read scope does not cause an error; the provider just reads an empty value. For example, `client_secret` is an empty string unless the application has the `read:client_keys` scope ([credentials doc](https://github.com/auth0/terraform-provider-auth0/blob/v1.63.0/docs/resources/client_credentials.md#L182)). Connection options need the scopes `read:connections_options` and `update:connections_options` ([options scope](https://auth0.com/docs/troubleshoot/product-lifecycle/deprecations-and-migrations/migrate-connection-options-scope)).\n\nAuth0 recommends one tenant for each environment, such as development, staging and production ([multiple environments](https://auth0.com/docs/get-started/auth0-overview/create-tenants/set-up-multiple-environments)). The IDs of objects differ from tenant to tenant, so configurations refer to objects through resources or data sources, never through copied IDs.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "one-tenant-one-identity"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "rectangle",
