    {
      "type": "text",
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 3239642060,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "id": "text-c2463087e13e",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "angle": 0,
      "x": 1288.8,
      "y": 380.0,
      "strokeColor": "#1E3A8A",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "width": 394.8,
      "height": 437.5,
      "seed": 983973,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Three Families of Resources\n| Family | Examples | Import ID | What a\ndestroy does |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Objects | `auth0_client`,\n`auth0_connection`, `auth0_action`,\n`auth0_log_stream` | The Auth0 ID, such as\n`con_\u2026` or `lst_\u2026` | Deletes the object |\n| Links | `auth0_connection_client`,\n`auth0_trigger_actions`, `auth0_client_grant`\n| Two IDs joined by `::`, such as\n`con_\u2026::<client ID>` | Removes the link |\n| Singletons | `auth0_tenant`,\n`auth0_branding`, `auth0_prompt`,\n`auth0_guardian` | Any random UUID | Differs\nby resource |\n\nThe import formats come from the Import\nsection of each [resource doc](https://github.\ncom/auth0/terraform-provider-auth0/tree/v1.63.\n0/docs/resources). A singleton is a setting\nthat exists once per tenant. Its destroy can\ndo nothing, delete something, or turn a\nprotection off; the pitfall Singletons on\nDestroy lists which.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-c2463087e13e",
      "originalText": "Three Families of Resources\n| Family | Examples | Import ID | What a destroy does |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Objects | `auth0_client`, `auth0_connection`, `auth0_action`, `auth0_log_stream` | The Auth0 ID, such as `con_\u2026` or `lst_\u2026` | Deletes the object |\n| Links | `auth0_connection_client`, `auth0_trigger_actions`, `auth0_client_grant` | Two IDs joined by `::`, such as `con_\u2026::<client ID>` | Removes the link |\n| Singletons | `auth0_tenant`, `auth0_branding`, `auth0_prompt`, `auth0_guardian` | Any random UUID | Differs by resource |\n\nThe import formats come from the Import section of each [resource doc](https://github.com/auth0/terraform-provider-auth0/tree/v1.63.0/docs/resources). A singleton is a setting that exists once per tenant. Its destroy can do nothing, delete something, or turn a protection off; the pitfall Singletons on Destroy lists which.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "three-families-of-resources"
      }
    },
    {
