      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "text": "Version Gaps and Deprecations\nAuth0 changes its API on a schedule, and old\nprovider versions fall behind it. For example,\nthe old way of managing the enabled clients of\na connection reached its end of life on\n2026-07-13 ([deprecations](https://auth0.com/d\nocs/troubleshoot/product-lifecycle/deprecation\ns-and-migrations)). Auth0 names provider\n1.29.0 or later as compatible with the new\nendpoints ([dedicated connection endpoints](ht\ntps://auth0.com/docs/troubleshoot/product-life\ncycle/deprecations-and-migrations/migrate-dedi\ncated-connection-endpoints)). The same page\nlists Rules and Hooks as deprecated in favor\nof actions. Read the changelog before each\nupgrade, and upgrade in steps.",
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 2,
      "textAlign": "center",
      "verticalAlign": "middle",
      "baseline": 17.5,
      "containerId": "node-1511f7055147",
      "originalText": "Version Gaps and Deprecations\nAuth0 changes its API on a schedule, and old provider versions fall behind it. For example, the old way of managing the enabled clients of a connection reached its end of life on 2026-07-13 ([deprecations](https://auth0.com/docs/troubleshoot/product-lifecycle/deprecations-and-migrations)). Auth0 names provider 1.29.0 or later as compatible with the new endpoints ([dedicated connection endpoints](https://auth0.com/docs/troubleshoot/product-lifecycle/deprecations-and-migrations/migrate-dedicated-connection-endpoints)). The same page lists Rules and Hooks as deprecated in favor of actions. Read the changelog before each upgrade, and upgrade in steps.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true,
      "customData": {
        "node_id": "auth0-version-gaps"
      }
    },
